        THE SELL-SIDE NDA. Parented by Disposition__c. Four states:
        Not Sent -> Sent -> Signed, plus Declined as a terminal off-ramp
        (Part 2 lines 28-41). Not Sent and Declined DID NOT EXIST on the field before
        2026-08-09; both are added by this tranche and neither is reachable from the
        acquisition record type.

        WHY A RECORD TYPE AT ALL (decision D7). NDA__c is already dual-parented - Opportunity__c
        for acquisitions, Disposition__c for dispositions - and the two sides need DIFFERENT
        state sets. One shared restricted picklist cannot express that: the acquisition path
        has no Not Sent and no decline off-ramp, and the disposition path has no Pending and no
        Received. Record types give per-type value sets and per-type Paths, so neither side
        sees the other's states.

        SENT AND SIGNED ARE SHARED WITH THE ACQUISITION TYPE. Unlike LOI__c.Stage__c, whose two
        sets are fully disjoint, THE NDA SETS OVERLAP - so Status__c ALONE DOES NOT IDENTIFY THE
        RECORD TYPE. Anything that must discriminate (a flexipage visibility rule, a report
        filter, a future Mark Declined action) has to test Disposition__c or RecordTypeId, never
        Status__c on its own.

