        🔴 NOTHING ABOUT THIS RECORD TYPE OR ITS RULE CHANGES - AND THE RULE IS STRENGTHENED, NOT
        WEAKENED. NDA__c was the cautionary exception ("unlike LOI"); LOI__c has now joined it, so
        this file's discipline - discriminate on Disposition__c or RecordTypeId, never on the
        status value alone - is now the DEFAULT for the acquisition/disposition object pairs
        rather than a special case. LOI_Record_Page paid for that in this same phase: its
        Submit_for_Approval entry keys on a stage value that is now shared, and it carries an
        open, undecided residual as a result (runbook 1.6 / gate G7).
        ⚠ DO NOT USE "the LOI sets are disjoint" AS PRIOR ART ANYWHERE AFTER THIS DATE. That
        sentence appears in several files; the ones found by sweep on 2026-08-14 are corrected,
        but this comment is the durable statement of the fact.

        WARNING - RECORD-TYPE PICKLIST RESTRICTION IS UI-ONLY. It is NOT enforced by Apex DML,
        so restricting Pending/Received out here does not stop a direct write. The Apex-side
        allow-list in RecordStageAdvanceService must become record-type-aware in the same
        tranche; that is the parallel developer change.

        THIS IS THE OFF-MARKET PATH'S FIRST STAGE. Disposition__c's Off_Market record type runs
        Disposition Readiness -> NDA -> Disposition Offer -> LOI -> PSA -> Closing -> Completed,
        so the NDA stage is where a direct sale actually starts, and the release gate
        All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression blocks EVERY forward stage from NDA onward until
        every NDA on the disposition is Signed (decision D15/Q4).

        DOCUSIGN IS NOT LICENSED YET (decision D2). These states are manually driven and the
        executed file is attached by hand; Method__c already carries a DocuSign value, so an
        envelope-status callback can later drive Status__c without reshaping this picklist or
        the gate that reads it.

        EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS ENUMERATED - Status__c, Method__c and Party_Role__c -
        because a record type file that omits a picklist silently drops all of its values from
        that type. Precedent: objects/Disposition__c/recordTypes/Off_Market.recordType-meta.xml.
        NDA__c has exactly three picklists after this tranche. Party_Role__c defaults to Buyer
        HERE and only here: DPEG collects one NDA from the prospective buyer and one from the
        introducing broker, and counter-signs both.

        No <businessProcess> - that element is for Opportunity, Case, Lead and Solution only.

        POST-DEPLOY, NOT DEPLOYABLE: profile record-type assignment (System Administrator
        included - Modify All Data is an OBJECT permission and confers no record-type access),
        the per-profile default, the layout assignment, and the migration of existing NDA rows
        off Master. profiles/** is .forceignore'd in this repo.

