        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-25 - 'Not Sent' REMOVED FROM THIS RECORD TYPE, AND THIS TYPE NOW HAS NO
        DEFAULT AT ALL. THIS FILE IS A CATCH-UP TO THE ORG, NOT A NEW DECISION.
        =====================================================================

        The user made the change in Setup first. Measured live via the UI API picklist-values
        endpoint for record type 012iw0000009yeaAAA (the ONLY channel that reports record-type-
        scoped values correctly - a RecordType retrieve returns fullName/active/description/label
        and STRIPS picklistValues, so a "clean sync from org" would silently delete every value
        block in this file): Status__c on this record type is exactly

            Prepare | Review | Approved | Sent | Signed | Declined      defaultValue: (empty)

        So the six-step sequence is now Prepare -> Review -> Approved -> Sent -> Signed, with
        Declined the terminal off-ramp. 'Not Sent' is gone from the MIDDLE of the sequence, which
        is the harder case to notice - see the 2026-08-14 amendment above, which makes exactly this
        point about LOI__c.

        🔴 'Not Sent' STAYS ACTIVE ON THE GLOBAL VALUE SET and stays on NOTHING ELSE. It was
        already restricted off Acquisition_NDA (see that file), so as of this change it is on NO
        record type in the org. It is therefore UNREACHABLE from any UI picker and, because
        NDA__c.Status__c is a RESTRICTED value set whose record-type subset DML DOES enforce
        (measured - see the 2026-08-20 correction in Acquisition_NDA), UNWRITABLE by Apex, Flow or
        the API on either type. Rows already sitting at 'Not Sent' in the org keep the value and
        still read fine; only new writes are refused. Everything downstream that merely READS the
        value - Tracking_Status__c's CASE, RecordStageAdvanceService's 'Not Sent' => 'Sent' hop,
        dispositionDealSummary's NDA_TONE map - was left in place ON PURPOSE, so those legacy rows
        keep rendering and advancing. Do not prune them as dead code.

        NO DEFAULT IS DELIBERATE AND IS THE ORG'S OWN STATE, not an omission in this file. A record
        type with no default leaves Status__c BLANK on a UI-created NDA and the user must pick.
        ⚠ CONSEQUENCE FOR APEX: DispositionStageEntryService cannot read a record-type default from
        a describe at any price (Apex exposes only the FIELD-level default), so it carries a
        constant, DISPOSITION_NDA_INITIAL_STATUS, which is now 'Prepare' - the first step of the
        sequence, chosen because a blank Status__c on an auto-created NDA would be indistinguishable
        from a failed creation. Keep that constant in step with the FIRST value listed below; there
        is no longer a <default>true</default> entry here to keep it in step with.

        WHAT ELSE MOVED IN THE SAME CHANGE (all repointed 'Not Sent' -> 'Prepare' as the disposition
